# Triaged findings. Everything here was checked against the image's own
# filesystem, not waved through: re-verify with
#   CID=$(docker create <image>); docker export "$CID" | tar -t | grep -E '/(mount|umount|nsenter|unshare)$'
#
# util-linux, via libuuid1. The image ships libuuid.so.1 (Python's uuid
# module links it) and none of the util-linux binaries — no mount,
# umount, nsenter, or unshare. All four advisories are flaws in those
# mount helpers, so the vulnerable code is not present. Trivy attributes
# them to libuuid1 because Debian builds it from the util-linux source
# package. Drop these entries the moment any util-linux binary enters
# the image.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410
